try’s lower-tier margins, highlighting a focus on volume and member value over pure margin expansion.\n\n### Release Quotes\n- [release line `00010`]: \"Net sales for the quarter increased 11.2 percent, to $93.9 billion, from $84.4 billion last year. Net sales for the fiscal year increased 10.1 percent, to $297.2 billion, from $269.9 billion last year.\"\n- [release line `00020`]: \"Net income for the fourth quarter was $2.998 billion, $6.75 per diluted share, compared to $2.610 billion, $5.87 per diluted share, last year. This year's fourth quarter was positively impacted by a non-recurring benefit of $0.15 per diluted share from IEEPA tariff refunds received in the quarter, less partial reinvestment of those refunds in increased member values. Net income for the fiscal year was $9.226 billion, $20.76 per diluted share, compared to $8.099 billion, $18.21 per diluted share, last year.\"\n\n### Notes\n- All figures are based on the most recent annual report (10-K) filed on 2026-10-07.\n- Peer companies' operating margins reflect their latest fiscal years as reported.",
